# Paths excluded from Draugr's own SAST self-scan. Semgrep reads this automatically when
# scanning this repo; it has no effect on scans Draugr runs for you.
#
# NOTE: providing this file *replaces* Semgrep's built-in ignore list rather than adding to it,
# so the defaults we still want are repeated here. Dropping them silently un-ignores test files
# and vendored code, which is how this file first went wrong.

# --- Semgrep's defaults, restored ---
.git/
node_modules/
vendor/
dist/
build/
tests/
test/
*_test.go
*.min.js
*.pyc

# --- Ours ---
# User-facing workflow templates. Semgrep's github-actions-mutable-action-tag rule wants every
# `uses:` pinned to a commit SHA. That's right for a workflow you operate and wrong for one you
# hand someone as a starting point: a SHA-pinned example can't be read at a glance, can't be
# maintained by whoever copies it, and rots the day the action releases. GitHub's own starter
# workflows use major tags for this reason, and contrib/starter-workflow is written to be
# submitted to that gallery.
#
# Draugr's real workflows, under .github/workflows/, are SHA-pinned and are still scanned.
examples/
contrib/starter-workflow/
